        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "HTTP Server (agentctl_web)\n└── Route Handler Registration\n    └── mux.HandleFunc(\"/api/sessions/\") \u003c-- 5a\n        └── SessionDetailHandler() \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/api/sessions.go:112\n            ├── Parse URL path\n            │   └── Extract session ID from path \u003c-- 5b\n            ├── Route to sub-handlers \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/api/sessions.go:134\n            │   ├── \"messages\" sub-route \u003c-- 5c\n            │   │   └── handlePersistedSessionMessages() \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/api/sessions.go:221\n            │   │       ├── sessions.Open() \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/api/sessions.go:241\n            │   │       ├── store.GetTurns() \u003c-- 5d\n            │   │       └── writeJSON(messages) \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/api/sessions.go:291\n            │   └── \"context-windows\" sub-route \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/api/sessions.go:139\n            │       └── handleSessionContextWindows() \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/api/sessions.go:301\n            │           ├── sessions.Open() \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/api/sessions.go:307\n            │           ├── store.GetContextWindows() \u003c-- 5e\n            │           └── writeJSON(windows) \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/api/sessions.go:340\n            └── Default: Get session detail \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/api/sessions.go:145\n                ├── sessions.Open() \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/api/sessions.go:151\n                ├── store.Get(sessionID) \u003c-- 5f\n                └── writeJSON(session) \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/api/sessions.go:167",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen users capture Claude Code conversations and store them in a database, they need a way to **retrieve and explore** that data programmatically. The session detail API endpoint solves this by exposing individual sessions and their sub-components (conversation turns, context windows) over HTTP [5a]. This enables web UIs, CLI tools, and other clients to **query session metadata, browse message history, and analyze context window boundaries** without direct database access.\n\n## Details\n\n### Route Registration and Dispatch\n\nThe web server registers `/api/sessions/` with a trailing slash to handle both detail requests and sub-routes [5a]. When a request arrives, the handler **parses the URL path** to extract the session ID [5b], then **dispatches based on the remaining path segments** [5c].\n\n### Sub-route: Messages\n\nThe `/api/sessions/{id}/messages` endpoint retrieves **conversation turns** from the `session_turns` table. It opens the sessions store per-request [5d], queries turns with pagination support, and returns them as a JSON array with metadata like role, content preview, tool calls, and error flags. This enables clients to **reconstruct the conversation flow** turn-by-turn.\n\n### Sub-route: Context Windows\n\nThe `/api/sessions/{id}/context-windows` endpoint fetches **compaction-bounded work spans** from the `session_context_windows` table [5e]. Each window represents work between context compaction events, with metadata about token counts, triggers, and chunk ranges. This supports **granular progressive memory retrieval** at a finer level than whole sessions.\n\n### Default: Session Detail\n\nWhen no sub-route is specified, the handler retrieves the **full session record** by ID [5f]. This includes summary, accomplished items, decisions, gotchas, tags, key files, token counts, and lineage fields (parent session, agent ID, status). The response is serialized to JSON with ISO 8601 timestamps.\n\n### Store Lifecycle\n\nEach handler **opens the sessions store independently** using `sessions.Open(r.Context(), cfg.Storage.Root)`, which connects to either SQLite or Turso based on configuration. The store is closed via `defer` after the response is written, ensuring **no connection pooling across requests** in this stateless design."
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "title": "Session Archive: Chunking and Context Windows",
      "description": "Skills layer - parses JSONL into chunks and context windows, compresses archive, and generates embeddings",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "6a",
          "path": "skills/session_archive/main.go",
          "lineNumber": 67,
          "lineContent": "sessionStore, cleanup, err := sessionkit.OpenSessions(ctx, rc.Config)",
          "title": "Open sessions store",
          "description": "Opens database for archival operations"
        },
        {
          "id": "6b",
          "path": "skills/session_archive/main.go",
          "lineNumber": 74,
          "lineContent": "session, err := sessionStore.Get(ctx, in.SessionID)",
          "title": "Retrieve session record",
          "description": "Fetches existing session or creates minimal record"
        },
        {
          "id": "6c",
          "path": "skills/session_archive/main.go",
          "lineNumber": 134,
          "lineContent": "result, err := archive.ChunkFile(jsonlPath, archive.ChunkOptions{SessionID: in.SessionID, MaxChunkSize: in.MaxChunkSize, SkipToChunk: skipToChunk, StartWindowIndex: startWindowIndex})",
          "title": "Parse and chunk JSONL",
          "description": "Splits conversation into chunks and identifies context windows"
        },
        {
          "id": "6d",
          "path": "skills/session_archive/main.go",
          "lineNumber": 199,
          "lineContent": "if err := sessionStore.SaveChunks(ctx, result.Chunks); err != nil {",
          "title": "Persist chunks",
          "description": "Bulk inserts chunks into session_chunks table"
        },
        {
          "id": "6e",
          "path": "skills/session_archive/main.go",
          "lineNumber": 204,
          "lineContent": "if err := sessionStore.SaveContextWindows(ctx, result.Windows); err != nil {",
          "title": "Persist context windows",
          "description": "Bulk inserts windows into session_context_windows table"
        },
        {
          "id": "6f",
          "path": "skills/session_archive/main.go",
          "lineNumber": 218,
          "lineContent": "embeddedCount, embeddingModel := embedContextWindows(ctx, sessionStore, savedWindows, result.Chunks, modelOverride)",
          "title": "Generate embeddings",
          "description": "Creates vector embeddings for each context window"
        },
        {
          "id": "6g",
          "path": "skills/session_archive/main.go",
          "lineNumber": 277,
          "lineContent": "if err := store.SetContextWindowEmbedding(ctx, window.ID, embeddingBytes, result.Model); err != nil {",
          "title": "Save window embedding",
          "description": "Updates context window with F32_BLOB vector"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Session Archive Skill Flow\n├── skill entry point (main) \u003c-- skills/session_archive/main.go:52\n│   └── sessionkit.OpenSessions() \u003c-- 6a\n│       └── sessions.Open() \u003c-- internal/sessionkit/open.go:20\n│           └── sqliteutil.OpenDB() \u003c-- internal/storage/sessions/store.go:95\n│               └── migrate() \u003c-- internal/storage/sessions/store.go:1704\n├── sessionStore.Get() \u003c-- 6b\n│   └── SELECT * FROM sessions WHERE id = ? \u003c-- internal/storage/sessions/store.go:228\n├── archive.ChunkFile() \u003c-- 6c\n│   ├── claudejsonl.OpenReader() \u003c-- skills/session_capture/main.go:106\n│   ├── parse messages into chunks\n│   └── identify context windows\n├── sessionStore.SaveChunks() \u003c-- 6d\n│   └── INSERT INTO session_chunks (batch) \u003c-- internal/storage/sessions/store.go:969\n├── sessionStore.SaveContextWindows() \u003c-- 6e\n│   └── INSERT INTO session_context_windows \u003c-- internal/storage/sessions/store.go:1182\n├── embedContextWindows() \u003c-- 6f\n│   ├── semantic.NewEmbedderWithModel() \u003c-- skills/session_archive/main.go:250\n│   ├── for each window \u003c-- skills/session_archive/main.go:262\n│   │   ├── buildWindowEmbeddingText() \u003c-- skills/session_archive/main.go:264\n│   │   ├── embedder.Embed() \u003c-- skills/session_archive/main.go:270\n│   │   └── store.SetContextWindowEmbedding() \u003c-- 6g\n│   │       └── UPDATE session_context_windows \u003c-- internal/storage/sessions/store.go:1318\n│   │           SET embedding = ?, model = ?\n│   └── return count, model \u003c-- skills/session_archive/main.go:284\n└── skillout.Emit() \u003c-- skills/session_archive/main.go:237",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nClaude Code conversations can span hundreds or thousands of messages, creating **massive JSONL files** that are slow to parse and impossible to search semantically. When you need to recall what happened in a previous session—what decisions were made, what errors occurred, or what context was relevant—you're forced to read through the entire archive linearly.\n\nThe **session archive skill** solves this by **chunking conversations into searchable units** called context windows. Each context window represents work between compaction boundaries (when Claude summarizes and clears its context). By storing these as separate database records with embeddings, you can later retrieve relevant portions of past conversations through semantic search, rather than parsing gigabytes of JSONL.\n\n## Details\n\n### Entry and Store Opening\n\nThe skill starts by opening the sessions database [6a], which contains the metadata record for this session [6b]. If the session doesn't exist yet, a minimal record is created with the workspace and JSONL path.\n\n### Chunking the JSONL\n\nThe core operation is `archive.ChunkFile()` [6c], which parses the JSONL file and splits it into **two key structures**:\n\n1. **Chunks**: Individual message segments (user requests, assistant responses, tool outputs, errors) with byte offsets for random access\n2. **Context windows**: Spans of chunks between compaction events, identified by `compact_boundary` messages with trigger metadata\n\nEach chunk tracks its type, tools used, files touched, and whether it contains errors. Context windows record their start/end times, pre-compaction token counts, and which chunks they contain.\n\n### Database Persistence\n\nChunks are bulk-inserted into `session_chunks` [6d] and context windows into `session_context_windows` [6e]. Both operations use **batch inserts with ON CONFLICT** clauses for idempotency—you can re-run the archive skill and it will only process new chunks/windows.\n\n### Embedding Generation\n\nIf `embed_windows=true`, the skill generates **vector embeddings for each context window** [6f]. It builds embedding text by filtering high-signal content (user requests, assistant responses, errors) while excluding noise (file contents, tool outputs, raw code). Each window's embedding is stored as an `F32_BLOB` column [6g], enabling fast cosine similarity searches later.\n\nThe embedding process uses the configured model (defaulting to the sessions scope model) and updates only the embedding field, preserving any existing summary text.\n\n### Result\n\nThe skill returns counts of chunks created, windows identified, and windows embedded, along with compression statistics if the JSONL was archived to gzip. This structured representation enables **progressive memory retrieval**—you can search for relevant context windows by semantic similarity rather than loading entire sessions."
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "title": "Web Server Initialization",
      "description": "Web server layer - starts HTTP server with route registration and middleware",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "7a",
          "path": "cmd/agentctl_web/main.go",
          "lineNumber": 69,
          "lineContent": "srv, err := web.NewServer(web.Options{Addr: addr, UIDir: uiDir, DevCORS: devCORS}, cfg, logger)",
          "title": "Create web server",
          "description": "Initializes server with config and logger"
        },
        {
          "id": "7b",
          "path": "cmd/agentctl_web/main.go",
          "lineNumber": 79,
          "lineContent": "go srv.Run(ctx)",
          "title": "Start SSE hub",
          "description": "Launches event broadcasting goroutine"
        },
        {
          "id": "7c",
          "path": "internal/interfaces/web/server.go",
          "lineNumber": 98,
          "lineContent": "mux.HandleFunc(\"/api/sessions\", api.SessionsListHandler(s.cfg, s.log))",
          "title": "Register sessions routes",
          "description": "Mounts list and detail handlers for session API"
        },
        {
          "id": "7d",
          "path": "internal/interfaces/web/server.go",
          "lineNumber": 152,
          "lineContent": "h := withCORS(s.opts.DevCORS, mux); h = withRequestLogging(s.log, h)",
          "title": "Apply middleware",
          "description": "Wraps handlers with CORS and logging"
        },
        {
          "id": "7e",
          "path": "cmd/agentctl_web/main.go",
          "lineNumber": 99,
          "lineContent": "if err := httpSrv.ListenAndServe(); err != nil \u0026\u0026 err != http.ErrServerClosed {",
          "title": "Start HTTP listener",
          "description": "Binds to port and begins serving requests"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Web Server Initialization (agentctl_web)\n├── main() entry point \u003c-- cmd/agentctl_web/main.go:38\n│   ├── Load config \u0026 setup logger \u003c-- cmd/agentctl_web/main.go:55\n│   ├── Create web server \u003c-- 7a\n│   │   └── web.NewServer() \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/server.go:26\n│   │       ├── Create SSE hub \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/server.go:27\n│   │       ├── Create console hub \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/server.go:28\n│   │       └── Return Server instance \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/server.go:42\n│   ├── Start SSE hub goroutine \u003c-- 7b\n│   ├── Build HTTP handler \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/server.go:61\n│   │   ├── Create mux \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/server.go:62\n│   │   ├── Register /api/sessions \u003c-- 7c\n│   │   ├── Register /api/sessions/ \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/server.go:99\n│   │   └── Apply middleware \u003c-- 7d\n│   │       ├── withCORS() \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/server.go:158\n│   │       └── withRequestLogging() \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/server.go:183\n│   └── Start HTTP server \u003c-- 7e\n└── Graceful shutdown on SIGINT/SIGTERM \u003c-- cmd/agentctl_web/main.go:107",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nThe **agentctl_web** server exposes agentctl's data stores (sessions, tasks, agents, etc.) through a **REST API** so that web UIs and external tools can query and visualize captured conversation data. Without this server, all data would be locked in local SQLite databases accessible only through CLI commands. The server solves the problem of **making session history and metadata available over HTTP** with proper routing, middleware, and real-time event streaming [7e].\n\n## Details\n\n### Initialization Flow\n\nThe server starts in `cmd/agentctl_web/main.go` [7a], which loads configuration and creates a `web.Server` instance. This server wraps an **SSE hub** for real-time events [7b] and a **console hub** for WebSocket connections. The core HTTP handler is built by `Handler()` [7d], which creates a `ServeMux` and registers all API routes.\n\n### Route Registration\n\nSession-related endpoints are mounted at `/api/sessions` (list) [7c] and `/api/sessions/` (detail with sub-routes). Each handler receives the config and logger, then **opens the sessions store on-demand per request** rather than holding a persistent connection. This pattern appears throughout: handlers call `sessions.Open(r.Context(), cfg.Storage.Root)` [4b] to get a fresh database connection for each HTTP request.\n\n### Middleware Stack\n\nBefore serving requests, the handler is wrapped with **CORS support** (for local development) and **request logging** [7d]. The `withCORS()` middleware adds appropriate headers for cross-origin requests, while `withRequestLogging()` logs each incoming request with method, path, and remote address.\n\n### Server Lifecycle\n\nAfter building the handler, `main()` starts the HTTP server with `ListenAndServe()` [7e]. The server runs until receiving SIGINT or SIGTERM, at which point it performs graceful shutdown by canceling the context (stopping the SSE hub) and calling `httpSrv.Shutdown()` with a 5-second timeout.\n\n### Design Philosophy\n\nThe architecture follows a **stateless handler pattern**: each request independently opens and closes database connections. This simplifies concurrency (no shared state) and ensures clean resource management, though it means paying connection overhead on every request. The trade-off favors correctness and simplicity over maximum throughput."
    }
  ],
  "description": "Maps session persistence from JSONL capture through SQLite/Turso storage to REST API exposure. Key flows include session capture [1e], schema migration [2b], vector search setup [3d], API list endpoint [4d], detail sub-routes [5c], and context window chunking [6c]. The system supports both local SQLite and cloud Turso with native vector search capabilities.",
  "mermaidDiagram": "graph TB\n    subgraph Skills[\"Skills Layer\"]\n        1a[\"1a: session_capture\u003cbr/\u003eskill entry\"]\n        1b[\"1b: open store\u003cbr/\u003evia sessionkit\"]\n        1e[\"1e: Save session\u003cbr/\u003eto database\"]\n        6a[\"6a: session_archive\u003cbr/\u003eopen store\"]\n        6c[\"6c: ChunkFile\u003cbr/\u003eparse JSONL\"]\n        6d[\"6d: SaveChunks\u003cbr/\u003epersist chunks\"]\n        6e[\"6e: SaveContextWindows\u003cbr/\u003epersist windows\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph SessionKit[\"Session Kit\"]\n        kit[\"sessionkit.OpenSessions\u003cbr/\u003eopens store from config\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Storage[\"Storage Layer\"]\n        interface[\"SessionStore\u003cbr/\u003einterface\"]\n        2a[\"2a: SQLite Open\u003cbr/\u003esessions.db\"]\n        2b[\"2b: sessions table\u003cbr/\u003eschema\"]\n        2e[\"2e: Upsert session\u003cbr/\u003eINSERT/UPDATE\"]\n        3a[\"3a: Turso Open\u003cbr/\u003elibsql connection\"]\n        3b[\"3b: F32_BLOB column\u003cbr/\u003evector storage\"]\n        3d[\"3d: Check vector\u003cbr/\u003eindex\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph API[\"Web API Layer\"]\n        7c[\"7c: Register routes\u003cbr/\u003e/api/sessions\"]\n        4b[\"4b: Open store\u003cbr/\u003eper request\"]\n        4d[\"4d: List sessions\u003cbr/\u003equery database\"]\n        4f[\"4f: Return JSON\u003cbr/\u003eresponse\"]\n        5b[\"5b: Extract ID\u003cbr/\u003efrom path\"]\n        5d[\"5d: GetTurns\u003cbr/\u003efetch messages\"]\n        5e[\"5e: GetContextWindows\u003cbr/\u003efetch windows\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph WebServer[\"Web Server\"]\n        7a[\"7a: NewServer\u003cbr/\u003einitialize\"]\n        7e[\"7e: ListenAndServe\u003cbr/\u003estart HTTP\"]\n    end\n\n    1a --\u003e 1b\n    1b --\u003e kit\n    kit --\u003e interface\n    interface --\u003e 2a\n    interface --\u003e 3a\n    1e --\u003e interface\n    \n    6a --\u003e kit\n    6c --\u003e 6d\n    6c --\u003e 6e\n    6d --\u003e interface\n    6e --\u003e interface\n\n    2a --\u003e 2b\n    2b --\u003e 2e\n    3a --\u003e 3b\n    3b --\u003e 3d\n\n    7a --\u003e 7c\n    7c --\u003e 4b\n    4b --\u003e kit\n    4d --\u003e interface\n    4f --\u003e 4d\n    5b --\u003e 5d\n    5b --\u003e 5e\n    5d --\u003e interface\n    5e --\u003e interface\n    7e --\u003e 7a\n\n    style Skills fill:#fcc2d7\n    style SessionKit fill:#ffec99\n    style Storage fill:#a5d8ff\n    style API fill:#b2f2bb\n    style WebServer fill:#d0bfff"
}